    <!-- Tab info dialogs -->
    <string name="tab_info_overview">Top events and screens show what your users do most. The daily chart tracks volume trends over the selected time window. All data is aggregated — no individual user is exposed.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_events">Raw event log in reverse chronological order. Each row represents one analytics event fired by the SDK. Use this to inspect props, screens, and metadata when debugging your integration.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_projects">Manage your projects and API keys. Each project has a unique API key — create separate projects for different apps, environments (dev/staging/prod), or platforms.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_settings">Toggle demo data for testing in debug mode. The demo switch only appears when the server runs in debug configuration. Production deployments hide this by default.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_flow">Screen transitions show how users navigate your app. Each row represents one common path from one screen to the next, grouped by session. High drop-off at a step may indicate UX friction — investigate why users leave at that point.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_live">Incoming events in real time. This feed auto-refreshes every few seconds to show the most recent events. Useful while integrating the SDK — watch events appear seconds after they fire in your app.</string>

